# Changesets versioning

When a change should ship, add a `.changeset/*.md` file (or `pnpm changeset`). Pick the bump from the work, not from commit count.

| Bump | Use when |
| --- | --- |
| **minor** | New feature, or a new tutorial / hobby article |
| **patch** | Bug fix (layout, a11y, typos, broken links, CI, deps that only fix bugs) |
| **major** | Site-wide UI redesign, or a tech-stack change (e.g. this Astro rewrite). Only with an explicit human request. |

Routine PRs use **minor** or **patch**. Do not add a `major` changeset unless the user asked to bump the major version.

```markdown
---
"vhnam.github.io": minor
---

Add hobby post: Chỉ định thử vài cuộn phim
```

Content-only article work is **minor**. A fix on an existing article is **patch**.
